@page "/privacy"
@attribute [AllowAnonymous]
@using ArchitectCoach.Web.Services.Privacy
@using Microsoft.Extensions.Options
@inject IOptions<SiteOptions> SiteOptionsAccessor

<PageTitle>Privacy notice · ArchitectCoach</PageTitle>

<article class="col-lg-9">
    <h1>Privacy notice</h1>
    <p class="muted">Last updated @Site.PrivacyNoticeUpdated</p>

    @if (!Site.IsConfigured)
    {
        <div class="alert alert-warning" role="note">
            Some operator details below haven't been configured yet. They must be filled in before this site is used publicly.
        </div>
    }

    <h2 class="h4">The short version</h2>
    <ul>
        <li>We keep your <strong>email address</strong>, a <strong>securely hashed password</strong>, and the <strong>projects</strong> you create. Nothing else about you.</li>
        <li>No analytics, no tracking cookies, no ads. We <strong>never sell or share</strong> your personal information.</li>
        <li>You can <a href="Account/Manage/PersonalData">download or delete everything</a> yourself, at any time.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2 class="h4">Who runs this site</h2>
    <p>
        @Or(Site.OperatorName) is responsible for this site and your data (the "controller" under GDPR).
        For any privacy question or request, email <strong>@Or(Site.PrivacyContactEmail)</strong>.
    </p>

    <h2 class="h4">What we collect, why, and for how long</h2>
    <div class="table-responsive">
        <table class="table">
            <caption class="visually-hidden">Personal data we hold, the reason, the legal basis, and how long it's kept</caption>
            <thead>
                <tr><th scope="col">Data</th><th scope="col">Why</th><th scope="col">Legal basis (GDPR)</th><th scope="col">Kept</th></tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody>
                <tr><th scope="row">Email address</th><td>Your sign-in, account confirmation, and password resets</td><td>Contract (to provide the service)</td><td>Until you delete your account. Unconfirmed accounts are deleted after 7 days.</td></tr>
                <tr><th scope="row">Hashed password, sign-in security data (failed-attempt count, optional two-factor and passkey keys)</th><td>Keeping your account secure</td><td>Contract</td><td>Until you delete your account</td></tr>
                <tr><th scope="row">Your projects (type, the one-line purpose you type, your answers, decision records)</th><td>The service itself</td><td>Contract</td><td>Until you delete the project or your account</td></tr>
                <tr><th scope="row">Sign-in and security cookies</th><td>Keeping you signed in; protecting forms from forgery</td><td>Strictly necessary (no consent needed)</td><td>Until you sign out, or up to 14 days</td></tr>
                <tr><th scope="row">Server logs (IP address, time, page requested)</th><td>Security and fixing problems</td><td>Legitimate interest</td><td>Our hosting provider's log retention; our own app logs never include your email, password, or project content</td></tr>
            </tbody>
        </table>
    </div>
    <p>Please don't put personal or confidential information in a project's purpose. It isn't needed.</p>

    <h2 class="h4">Who else handles your data</h2>
    <p>
        Our hosting provider (SmarterASP.NET) runs the website, database, and email sending on our behalf, as our
        processor. Data is stored in: <strong>@Or(Site.HostingRegion)</strong>. If you're in the EU or UK and your data
        is stored outside it, the transfer relies on the safeguards our provider offers (such as standard contractual
        clauses). We use no other third parties.
    </p>

    <h2 class="h4">Your rights</h2>
    <p>Wherever you live, you can:</p>
    <ul>
        <li><strong>See and download</strong> everything we hold: <a href="Account/Manage/PersonalData">Personal data → Download</a> (GDPR access and portability; CCPA right to know).</li>
        <li><strong>Correct</strong> it: change your email under <a href="Account/Manage/Email">Account → Email</a>, or edit or delete projects.</li>
        <li><strong>Delete</strong> it: delete single projects, or your whole account under <a href="Account/Manage/PersonalData">Personal data → Delete</a>. Deletion is immediate and permanent.</li>
        <li><strong>Object or restrict</strong> processing, or ask any question, by emailing @Or(Site.PrivacyContactEmail). We answer within one month (45 days for California requests).</li>
        <li><strong>Complain</strong> to your data protection authority if you think we've handled your data wrongly.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>We don't sell or share personal information (as CCPA defines those terms), don't use it for advertising or profiling, and won't treat you differently for using any of these rights.</p>

    <h2 class="h4">Children</h2>
    <p>This site is not for children. You must be 16 or older to create an account.</p>

    <h2 class="h4">Security and breaches</h2>
    <p>
        Connections are encrypted (HTTPS). Passwords are stored only as salted, slow hashes. Accounts lock after repeated
        failed sign-ins. If a breach ever puts your data at risk, we'll tell you and the relevant authorities as the law requires.
    </p>

    <h2 class="h4">Changes</h2>
    <p>If this notice changes in a way that matters, we'll update the date above and tell signed-in users.</p>
</article>

@code {
    private SiteOptions Site => SiteOptionsAccessor.Value;

    private static string Or(string value) => string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(value) ? "[not yet configured]" : value;
}
